> Required Notice: Copyright Yoyodyne, Inc. (http://example.com)

## Anti-reverse-engineering

You may not reverse engineer, decompile, or disassemble the
software, except to the extent that this restriction is
forbidden by applicable law.

## Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose.  A
noncommercial purpose is a purpose other than direct or
indirect commercial advantage or monetary compensation.

## Commercial Purposes

Commercial purposes are not permitted purposes.  For example,
commercial purposes include:

* using the software in an enterprise for business operations
* using the software to provide commercial services
* selling access to or use of the software
* distributing the software as part of a commercial product

## Fair Use

You may have rights under the law, such as fair use, that
this license does not restrict.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not grant you any right to use the licensor's
trademarks, trade names, or service marks, or other than the
copyright licenses granted above.

## Defense of Claims

If someone makes a claim against the licensor or another
licensee for copyright infringement related to the software,
and you have a copyright license from that same licensor,
then your copyright license is suspended while that claim
is pending.  If you defend the claim, or the claim is
dismissed or settled, your copyright license is restored.

## Termination

If you fail to comply with these terms, your license is
terminated immediately.  If you fix your failure within 30
days of when you first learn of it, your license will be
restored, but the licensor can terminate your license
permanently if you have violated these terms before.

## No Liability

As far as the law allows, the software is provided as is,
without any warranty or condition, and the licensor will not
be liable to you for any damages arising out of these terms
or the use or nature of the software, under any kind of
legal claim.

## Definitions

The **licensor** is the individual or entity offering these
terms, and the **software** is the software the licensor
makes available under these terms.

You are the individual or entity taking up the software
under these terms.

Your **licenses** are all your licenses from the licensor
